    "mapping_notes": "# tensorrt_llm__cutlass_mixed_runner_bf16_int4_gemm_fg_scaleonly__sm_100f\n\n## Reference interface\n\nAll indices below are logical indices. Byte-level layout information from the\nsaved optimized input is retained in source_interface.\n\n| Parameter | Type | Logical shape | Role | Optimized counterpart |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| A | bf16 | 128 x 64 | input | logical activation A |\n| B | uint8_t | 128 x 32 | input | logical weight B; reference rows are output channels |\n| D | bf16 | 128 x 128 | output | D |\n| scale | bf16 | 128 x 1 | input | per-output-channel, per-K-group weight scale |\n\n## Computation and mapping\n\nThe reference uses A[m,k], B[n,k], and D[m,n]; B is stored with output-channel first.\nB is canonical signed INT4: even k in the low nibble, odd k in the high nibble.\nweight[n,k] = signed_int4(B[n,k]) * scale[n,k/64].\nD[m,n] = sum_k A[m,k] * weight[n,k]. No zero-point is used.\nThe selected SM100 source uses signed int4 with contiguous K coordinates.\nThe byte mapping preserves the two adjacent nibbles; signed decoding remains\npart of the expressions. No host-side weight permutation is applied by this mapping.\nScale layout [n,k_group] is the transpose of source [k_group,n] storage.\nThe optimized mainloop swaps/transposes operands. The reference restores\nactivation-first GEMM; its M/N names are the public mathematical M/N names.\nThe saved epilogue uses alpha=1 and beta=0; C is not read.\n\n## Validation boundary\n\nNot compared against an optimized GPU execution.\nPrecision/reduction-order differences follow\nthe mathematical contract in the top-level README.\n\n## Upstream\n\n- https://github.com/NVIDIA/TensorRT-LLM/blob/ef567dd9b8919f6ee8b2da1f6f6d0c90206a78f8/cpp/tensorrt_llm/kernels/cutlass_kernels/fpA_intB_gemm/launchers/fpA_intB_launcher_sm100.inl\n- https://github.com/NVIDIA/TensorRT-LLM/blob/ef567dd9b8919f6ee8b2da1f6f6d0c90206a78f8/cpp/tensorrt_llm/cutlass_extensions/include/cutlass_extensions/gemm/collective/sm100_mma_warpspecialized_mixed_input.hpp\n"
  },
